## HOW TO PLAY
## ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
howtoplay.category.project_bee=Project Bee
howtoplay.pb.s_a.p=§eProject Bee§r is a bee automation addon. You catch bees, house them in an §bAdvanced Beehive§r, collect their combs and turn them into resources.
howtoplay.pb.s_loop.h=The Loop
howtoplay.pb.s_loop.p=§b1.§r Catch a bee with a §bBee Cage§r (swing at it), or find one in a nest.\n§b2.§r Put the filled cage in an §bAdvanced Beehive§r with flowers nearby.\n§b3.§r Take the combs from the output grid.\n§b4.§r Process combs in a §bPowered Centrifuge§r for resources and Wax.\n§b5.§r Breed rarer bees in the §bBreeding Chamber§r and grow babies in the §bBee Incubator§r.
howtoplay.pb.s_know.h=Good to Know
howtoplay.pb.s_know.p=§7•§r A hive makes §e3 combs§r per cycle (99% chance). The cycle is 100 ticks (5 s).\n§7•§r Bees like Bee, Biomass, Bumble, Leaf Cutter, Blue Banded and Blue Mason need flowers within 5 blocks. Others don't.\n§7•§r Bred bees are §cbabies§r. Babies can't be released until the Incubator grows them up.\n§7•§r Machines use §eDE (Dorios Energy)§r.\n§7•§r §6Addon Bees§r drop items (ingots, shards) from companion addons. Without those addons the items won't exist.
howtoplay.pb.s_pages.h=Chapters
howtoplay.pb.s_pages.p=§7Natural Bees§r — wild and easy bees\n§7Resource Bees§r — ore, gem and mob bees\n§7Addon Bees§r — alloy and advanced bees\n§7Finding Bees§r — catching, spawns, nests, conversion\n§7Breeding§r — every cross with pictures\n§7Machines§r — every machine and troubleshooting\n§7Items & Upgrades§r — cages, treats, upgrades, recipes
howtoplay.pb:start=Start Here
howtoplay.pb:start.title=Project Bee - Start Here
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_i.p=The vanilla Bee and Project Bee's own natural species. Start here: most are found in the wild or in nests.
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_vanilla.h=Bee
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_vanilla.p=§7Comb:§r §eHoneycomb§r (3 per cycle, 99%)\n§7Centrifuge:§r §b§r + Wax · 8,000 DE · 4s\n§7Incubator:§r 10 Honey Treats\n§7Nests:§r Oak Bee Nest, Birch Bee Nest, Spruce Bee Nest\n§7Needs:§r flowers within 5 blocks of the hive
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_bumble.h=Bumble Bee
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_bumble.p=§7Comb:§r §eBumble Comb§r (3 per cycle, 99%)\n§7Centrifuge:§r §bHoney Bottle 30%§r + Wax · 8,000 DE · 4s\n§7Incubator:§r 20 Honey Treats\n§7Found:§r Spawns on the surface in grassy (animal) biomes, in daylight.\n§7Nests:§r Acacia Bee Nest\n§7Bred from:§r Bee + Bee (30%)\n§7Needs:§r flowers within 5 blocks of the hive
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_leaf_cutter.h=Leaf Cutter Bee
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_leaf_cutter.p=§7Comb:§r §eLeaf Cutter Comb§r (3 per cycle, 99%)\n§7Centrifuge:§r §bOak Leaves x2 70%§r + Wax · 6,000 DE · 3s\n§7Incubator:§r 20 Honey Treats\n§7Found:§r Spawns on the surface in grassy (animal) biomes, in daylight.\n§7Nests:§r Spruce Bee Nest\n§7Bred from:§r Bee + Bee (20%)\n§7Needs:§r flowers within 5 blocks of the hive\n§7Simulator food:§r Oak Leaves, Birch Leaves, Spruce Leaves, Jungle Leaves, Acacia Leaves, Dark Oak Leaves
howtoplay.pb.nat_bees_blue_banded.h=Blue Banded Bee
